{"metadata":{"externalID":"Tries","symbolKind":"module","title":"Tries","modules":[{"name":"Tries"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection"},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Tries over sequences of any ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" symbols, with prefix queries, and multi-pattern matching.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sets-of-sequences","title":"Sets of sequences","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree"]},{"anchor":"Dictionaries-keyed-by-sequences","title":"Dictionaries keyed by sequences","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary"]},{"anchor":"Pattern-matching","title":"Pattern matching","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton"]},{"anchor":"Extended-Modules","title":"Extended Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trees"],"generated":true}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tries"]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie"},{"type":"text","text":" is a set of sequences and a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary"},{"type":"text","text":" a dictionary keyed by them, both kept in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a trie (Fredkin, 1960): a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose root-to-vertex paths spell the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keys. They answer the queries a hash set cannot: every key with a prefix"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"elements(withPrefix:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", whose "},{"code":"count","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is O(1)), whether any key has one ("},{"code":"hasPrefix(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the longest key that is a prefix of a query ("},{"code":"longestPrefix(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import Tries","","let words = Trie([\"car\", \"cart\", \"cat\", \"dog\"])","words.contains(\"cat\")                                   \/\/ true","words.elements(withPrefix: \"car\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ [\"car\", \"cart\"]","words.longestPrefix(of: \"carton\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ \"cart\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keys are any sequence of the symbol type and are stored as ","type":"text"},{"code":"[Symbol]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". For text, the symbol","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type decides what a step is: ","type":"text"},{"code":"Trie<Character>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" steps by grapheme cluster, ","type":"text"},{"code":"Trie<Unicode.Scalar>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by scalar, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Trie<UInt8>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" over ","type":"text"},{"code":"utf8","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by byte, the fastest of the three, because comparing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bytes is cheaper than comparing ","type":"text"},{"code":"Character","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s. When the symbols are ","type":"text"},{"code":"Comparable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", each vertex keeps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its children sorted, so iteration is in lexicographic order; otherwise children come in the order","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"they were added.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" hold the same keys and answer the same queries,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with the same names, in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): every chain of vertices with one child and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its symbols, so there is a vertex per key and per","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"branching point rather than per symbol. They suit keys with long shared prefixes, such as file","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"paths or URLs, and build faster and in less memory than a trie of the same keys.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A trie’s shape converts to Grafluent’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrefixTree"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrefixTree(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and a radix tree’s to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence"},{"type":"text","text":" of its vertices’ prefixes with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (import Grafluent’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trees"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module beside this one)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (Aho and Corasick, 1975) finds every occurrence of any of a set of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patterns in one pass over a text, in O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":" + "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"z"}]},{"type":"text","text":") for "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":" symbols and "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"z"}]},{"type":"text","text":" matches: a trie of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patterns with failure links. Its "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/statesView-swift.property","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is the automaton as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let automaton = AhoCorasickAutomaton(patterns: [\"he\", \"she\", \"his\", \"hers\"])","automaton.matches(in: \"ushers\").map(\\.patternIndex)   \/\/ [1, 0, 3]"]}]}],"references":{"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/TrieDictionary":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrieDictionary"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrieDictionary"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A dictionary keyed by sequences, kept in a trie: a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"root-to-vertex paths spell the keys, each key’s vertex holding its value (Fredkin, 1960)."}],"url":"\/documentation\/tries\/triedictionary","title":"TrieDictionary","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/AhoCorasickAutomaton/statesView-swift.property":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"statesView"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Tries20AhoCorasickAutomatonV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":">."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"StatesView","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Tries20AhoCorasickAutomatonV10StatesViewV"}],"conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Symbol"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/statesView-swift.property","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The automaton’s states as a directed graph: a vertex per state, numbered from 0 for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"root, a goto edge from each state to each of its trie children, and a failure edge from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each state but the root to its failure state. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/StatesView-swift.struct\/symbol(ofEdgeAt:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" tells the two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"apart."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"statesView","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/ahocorasickautomaton\/statesview-swift.property"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/AhoCorasickAutomaton":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/ahocorasickautomaton","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An automaton that finds every occurrence of every pattern of a set in one pass over a text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(Aho and Corasick, 1975)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton"}],"title":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton"}]},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries","abstract":[{"text":"Tries over sequences of any ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" symbols, with prefix queries, and multi-pattern matching.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/tries","title":"Tries","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/RadixTreeDictionary":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A dictionary keyed by sequences, kept in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): a trie in which every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"chain of vertices with one child and no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"symbols, each key’s vertex holding its value."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/radixtreedictionary","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RadixTreeDictionary","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"RadixTreeDictionary","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RadixTreeDictionary","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/AhoCorasickAutomaton/StatesView-swift.struct/symbol(ofEdgeAt:)":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The symbol a goto edge reads, or nil for a failure edge."}],"url":"\/documentation\/tries\/ahocorasickautomaton\/statesview-swift.struct\/symbol(ofedgeat:)","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/StatesView-swift.struct\/symbol(ofEdgeAt:)","role":"symbol","title":"symbol(ofEdgeAt:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"ofEdgeAt"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/Trie":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/trie","abstract":[{"text":"A set of sequences kept in a trie: a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose root-to-vertex","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"paths spell the keys (Fredkin, 1960).","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Trie"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie","title":"Trie","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Trie"}]},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/Trees":{"role":"collection","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trees","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","title":"Trees","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/trees"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/RadixTree":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RadixTree","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RadixTree","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A set of sequences kept in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): a trie in which every chain of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices with one child and no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its symbols.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/tries\/radixtree","title":"RadixTree","kind":"symbol"}}}